                "expected_hash": "53efb1ac938660db3b882526795a4a92d7ff0b96355f16850e086548ae467915",
                "edits": [
                  {
                    "old_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities.\n",
                    "new_text": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities for working with numbers and labels.\n\n## `numbers.total(values)`\n\n`total` returns the sum of numeric values in an iterable, ignoring any\n`None` entries. Zero and negative numbers are included in the sum.\n\n- If the iterable is empty, the result is `0`.\n- If the iterable contains only `None`, the result is also `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## `labels.normalize(value)`\n\n`normalize` removes leading and trailing whitespace from a string and\nconverts the remaining characters to lowercase. Internal spaces are\npreserved.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")  # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")     # \"\"\n```\n"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
