  "final_files": {
    "numbers.py": "def total(values):\n    return sum(value for value in values if value is not None)\n",
    "labels.py": "def normalize(value):\n    \"\"\"Normalize a string by trimming leading/trailing whitespace and\n    converting it to lowercase. Internal spaces are preserved.\n\n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> normalize(' A B ')\n    'a b'\n    >>> normalize('  ')\n    ''\n    \"\"\"\n    return value.strip().lower()\n",
    "README.md": "# Helpers\n\nUtilities for working with numbers and labels.\n\n## `numbers.total(values)`\n\n`total` returns the sum of numeric values in an iterable, ignoring any\n`None` entries. Zero and negative numbers are included in the sum.\n\n- If the iterable is empty, the result is `0`.\n- If the iterable contains only `None`, the result is also `0`.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom numbers import total\n\ntotal([2, None, -1, 0])  # 1\ntotal([None])            # 0\ntotal([])                # 0\n```\n\n## `labels.normalize(value)`\n\n`normalize` removes leading and trailing whitespace from a string and\nconverts the remaining characters to lowercase. Internal spaces are\npreserved.\n\nExamples:\n\n```python\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nnormalize(\" A B \")  # \"a b\"\nnormalize(\"  \")     # \"\"\n```\n",
    "test_numbers.py": "import unittest\nfrom numbers import total\n\nclass NumbersTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_total(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([2, None, -1, 0]), 1)\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(total([None]), 0)\n",
    "test_labels.py": "import unittest\nfrom labels import normalize\n\nclass LabelsTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_normalize(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize(' A B '), 'a b')\n    def test_empty(self):\n        self.assertEqual(normalize('  '), '')\n"
